      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change breaks the libvnet ABI contract with downstream consumers of VPP. Out-of-tree plugins accessing symbols removed from the shared object file will break. IMHO, this is not acceptable in the present form.\n\nThere needs to be a migration plan analogous to the Production API change process [0] for ABI changes.  It would be best add a document to the repository defining the ABI breaking change policy in this gerrit change and reviewing it both on vpp-dev@lists.fd.io and in a VPP Community meeting prior to merging this change.\n\nRecommended subjects to be included are:\n\n1. Definition of breaking ABI changes\n2. Build time ABI compliance checking for in-tree and out-of-tree plugins\n3. Opt-in mechanism for new ABI behavior (i.e. retention of old ABI as default)\n4. Retention period for previous ABI behavior\n5. Duration of opt-in period prior to making new ABI behavior the default",
